;; Reviewed 2026-10-11 by the user (written by Claude, from the design,
;; the MACRO manual, LLVM's code generator and the guest runs). Why this
;; is right:
;; - Phase 16 step 5 (section 16, proposal 7): SYSTEM.VAL(HUGEINT, x),
;;   x narrower, which Val did not lower. As LLVM's GenerateVal: x's
;;   bytes widened to the quadword, sign-extended if x is an integer (a
;;   SHORTINT, an INTEGER, a LONGINT, an ADDRESS: sext), zero-extended
;;   otherwise (a CHAR, a SET, a pointer: zext).
;; - The low longword is x moved (MOVL) or widened (CVTBL, CVTWL,
;;   MOVZBL) into R0, the result's register pair; the high longword is
;;   its sign, ASHL #-31, R0, R1, or 0, CLRL R1.
;; - ToAddress, ToChar and ToSet are the narrowing and same-size cases
;;   Val already lowered: the low longword or byte of the value, read in
;;   place, and a longword retyped.
;; - ValOut, run on the guest, prints what the LLVM build prints
;;   (output.expected).
